; Sprite set unpack records: 20 records of 6 bytes, one per packed sprite set
;
; Record n tells the unpacker #R$AF15 how to turn the packed set n (room script op $97 n, #R$A146) into the sprite
; sheet at #R$D700. The sheet is a page per pixel row (the high byte of an address is the pixel row, the low byte the
; byte column) and a sprite is a run of columns read down the pages. The 20 records and what they hold:
; .
; +0 word: destination in the sheet: page = first pixel row ($D7 row 0, $EF row 24), low byte = first byte column; the
; columns go up from there (INC E: never a carry into the page); the sets one room uses have different destinations,
; sets of different rooms reuse them (several start at $D763)
; +2 word: address of the packed set (#R$68CC..#R$7169, label PackedSetN)
; +4 byte: flags. Bit 7: after each frame add three copies shifted right by 2, 4 and 6 pixels (the entities are
; positioned in 2-pixel steps, so a sprite is drawn from the copy for x AND 3). Bit 6: after all frames add the mirrored
; copy of every frame (columns reversed and each byte bit-reversed through the table #R$C500 that #R$BE48 builds on room
; entry), used for the other walking direction. Other bits unused
; +5 byte: frame width in columns (the packed set holds frames x width columns)
; .
; The sheet bytes written by #R$AF15 for all 20 records agree with a model of the format described here (see finding
; F114).
@label=UnpackRecords
b$AE9D DEFW $D7F8,$68CC ; set 0: skeleton archers (rooms 17, 21)
 $AEA1 DEFB $40,$02
 $AEA3 DEFW $D763,$6916 ; set 1: crusaders (rooms 0, 4, 5, 6, 24, 25)
 $AEA7 DEFB $C0,$02
 $AEA9 DEFW $D763,$6979 ; set 2: Death (room 18)
 $AEAD DEFB $C0,$04
 $AEAF DEFW $D7BB,$6AA7 ; set 3: red winged devils (rooms 21, 22)
 $AEB3 DEFB $C0,$02
 $AEB5 DEFW $EF63,$6B02 ; set 4: magenta winged flyers (rooms 20, 23)
 $AEB9 DEFB $C0,$03
 $AEBB DEFW $D768,$6B46 ; set 5: unidentified, room 10 (Pestilent Beast)
 $AEBF DEFB $00,$02
 $AEC1 DEFW $D763,$6BDA ; set 6: head of the Pestilent Beast (room 10); frame width 5, but the set has only 4 columns
 $AEC5 DEFB $00,$05
 $AEC7 DEFW $D7E7,$6C4F ; set 7: red whirling fireballs (rooms 22, 23)
 $AECB DEFB $00,$02
 $AECD DEFW $D763,$6C7B ; set 8: green flies (room 12)
 $AED1 DEFB $40,$02
 $AED3 DEFW $D76B,$6CB6 ; set 9: green flies, second kind (room 12)
 $AED7 DEFB $40,$02
 $AED9 DEFW $D763,$6CF1 ; set 10: hanged men (room 9)
 $AEDD DEFB $40,$02
 $AEDF DEFW $D763,$6D1D ; set 11: green zombies (rooms 15, 20)
 $AEE3 DEFB $C0,$02
 $AEE5 DEFW $D763,$6D80 ; set 12: grinning cyan ghost (room 11)
 $AEE9 DEFB $C0,$02
 $AEEB DEFW $D763,$6DC6 ; set 13: rats (room 2)
 $AEEF DEFB $C0,$02
 $AEF1 DEFW $D78F,$6DF5 ; set 14: Satan's pieces (room 24)
 $AEF5 DEFB $00,$1E
 $AEF7 DEFW $D763,$7042 ; set 15: red bats (room 8)
 $AEFB DEFB $80,$02
 $AEFD DEFW $D7EA,$7074 ; set 16: scythe pieces, probably (room 18)
 $AF01 DEFB $80,$02
 $AF03 DEFW $D763,$70B7 ; set 17: skeletons (rooms 13, 22)
 $AF07 DEFB $C0,$02
 $AF09 DEFW $D78F,$710E ; set 18: white ghosts (rooms 22, 23)
 $AF0D DEFB $C0,$02
 $AF0F DEFW $D7F5,$7169 ; set 19: cyan worms (rooms 9, 14)
 $AF13 DEFB $80,$02
